                <pb facs="1153" n="1141" sameAs="frus:frus1940v05/pg1141"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">823.51/1388a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in Peru</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">McGurk</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-12-16T20:00:00-05:00">December 16, 1940—8
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>149. The Export-Import Bank has approved the extension of a credit of $10,000,000
                    to the Central Reserve Bank of Peru at 4 percent <pb facs="1154" n="1142"
                        xml:id="pg1142"/> interest and to be amortized over a 6 year period. The
                    proceeds of the credit are to be used for general imports of United States
                    goods, and the earlier $2,000,000 credit is to be canceled. Details of the
                    arrangement are being worked out with Beltrán, and no public announcement is to
                    be made at this time.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
